{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.ordinary_word_primary","record":{"id":"circuit.ordinary_word_primary","kind":"goal","label":"Primary-route finite ordinary near-optimal word","status":"unverified","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-assembly","locator":"06-assembly.tex:1–34; proof of thm:main","statement":"For every ε>0, a finite ordinary cost/mixer word W, with deterministic real angles independent of D,n,J, has rooted energy greater than P_*−ε. Choose the classical input with error ε/4 and η_H=(ε/8)²; choose synthesis η=ε/8, so its two losses sum to less than ε/2; then remove the seed with error less than ε/4.","assumption_ids":[],"evidence_ids":[],"citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-ordinary-word-primary"],"boundary":"This is an existence statement for one common finite word. Cost gates, mixers, identity padding and combining adjacent equal gate types convert it to the standard alternating QAOA convention. The tree-to-SK step is still a separate theorem."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.ordinary_word_primary","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/69473417dc487cafa5e2e39b3168d2c4a8bffdad2e91b6e486de48f122dda071","roles":["mapped_claim"]},{"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/77f0cf29ab577b42d8caa5b2831ebfb1ca170d4b13c1ef6897cadc8e93c2a834","roles":["recorded_prerequisite"]},{"stage":"expository","subgraph_ref":"sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json/support/0.3.1/9dd5536bc567fc55efaa864733bf89747cea0268a8a3865dec51ddd8e2a235dd","roles":["recorded_prerequisite"]}],"direct_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/qaoa-assembly","anchor":"qaoa-assembly","mapping_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids"}]},"aligned_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/qaoa-assembly","anchor":"qaoa-assembly","mapping_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids","text":"\n\n<a id=\"qaoa-assembly-detail\"></a>\n\n### 8.6 Fixing the word before the thermodynamic limit\n\nAllocate errors after choosing the desired $\\varepsilon>0$. Apply the\nclassical near-optimality proposition with the two tolerances\n$\\varepsilon/4$ and $\\eta_H=(\\varepsilon/8)^2$. It supplies one\nformula and its helper law together, with classical loss below\n$\\varepsilon/4$ and $0<p_H<\\eta_H$. In its proof the uncoloured\nformula is fixed first, then the small positive helper probabilities\nand the excluded-colour approximation are selected. Thus changing a\nhelper law does not silently preserve an already fixed formula. With\n$\\eta=\\varepsilon/8$, synthesis gives\n$$\n\\mathcal E(v)\\ge\\mathcal E(m)-2\\eta-2\\sqrt{p_H}\n >P_*-3\\varepsilon/4.\n$$\nSeed removal uses less than $\\varepsilon/4$. The resulting fixed\nordinary word therefore satisfies $v_W>P_*-\\varepsilon$ after the\nfixed-word transfer. Its thermodynamic limit is taken only after\nall approximation choices have been made. Since $Q_p\\le P_*$ and\nzero padding makes $Q_p$ nondecreasing, this proves the source's\nthermodynamic-first conclusion from its stated analytic inputs.\n[OpenAI (2026b), §6][q-assembly].\n\nThe order is: accuracy; minimizer and fixed $T<1$; finite scalar mesh;\nsmoothing and bounded approximations; finite types and positive helper\nmasses; exact helper contractions and finite commutator products; one\nfixed seeded word; initialization size; generic angle perturbation;\nfinite selective pulse lists; sufficiently small $r$; one ordinary\nword; its $n\\to\\infty$ limit. The degree limits identify the rooted\ncalculus and the transferred value for each already fixed word; they\ndo not license changing that word with the finite instance.\n\nThe reconstruction makes the source's circuit mechanisms explicit,\nbut the evidence classes remain separate. The scalar construction\nand its formal interfaces in §§6–7 and 12 do not by themselves establish the\nweighted unitary calculus, simultaneous helper contraction or seed\nremoval. Those analytic theorems are additional inputs from the QAOA\nmanuscript, with the domain, commutation and uniformity hypotheses\nspecified above. No quantitative depth bound, finite-size rate,\nefficient angle-selection procedure, or independent formal\nverification of this entire circuit construction follows from the\nselected formal statements.\n\nThis completes the main support-to-circuit proof. The later comparisons\nhave separate purposes: [§11.1](#positive-temperature-route)\ngives another classical input; [§11.2](#fixed-word-probability) adds a\nsecond-moment sampling theorem; and [§§11.3–11.5](#depth-quantifiers)\ncompare quantifiers, other models and later finite-size estimates. They\nare not further premises of the proof just completed.\n","span":{"start_byte":150001,"end_byte":152749,"start_line":3283,"end_line":3335},"paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=qaoa-assembly","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=qaoa-assembly"}],"lenses":{"prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=circuit.ordinary_word_primary&assumptions=true","consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=circuit.ordinary_word_primary&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&node=circuit.ordinary_word_primary&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&node=circuit.ordinary_word_primary&relation=prerequisites"},"relations":[{"family":"arguments","id":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/edges/%5B%22circuit.high_girth_maxcut%22%2C%22circuit.ordinary_word_primary%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","from":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.high_girth_maxcut","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.ordinary_word_primary","kind":"supports","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","derived":false,"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/edges/%5B%22circuit.high_girth_maxcut%22%2C%22circuit.ordinary_word_primary%22%2C%22supports%22%5D"},{"family":"arguments","id":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/edges/%5B%22circuit.ordinary_word_primary%22%2C%22circuit.classical_primary%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","from":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.ordinary_word_primary","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.classical_primary","kind":"supports","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","derived":false,"record_ref":"sha2